   "evidence": "A grep for `ofBaseSet_ofBaseSet|theorem ofBaseSet_|ofBaseSet_eq` in code/TauCeti finds nothing. BundleMap.lean comments: '-- The atlas `(A.ofBaseSet h).ofBaseSet _` of `V` has the fields of `A`, so it is `A`.' (bundleEquivL, tangentHomEquivL) and '-- \u2026 whose own `ofBaseSet` atlas of `V` has the fields of `A`.' (chartValueL_bundleEquivL_symm_ae_coord, chartValueL_tangentHomEquivL_symm_ae_coord).",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle/Sobolev/BundleMap.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] theorem FiniteBundleAtlas.ofBaseSet_ofBaseSet : (A.ofBaseSet h).ofBaseSet h' = A` next to `image_ofBaseSet` in FiniteBundleAtlas/Basic.lean, provable by `(rfl)` or structure eta. Cite it instead of the 'has the fields of `A`' comments.",
   "issue": "`coe_bundleEquivL_symm` and `bundleEquivL_symm_apply` (and the `tangentHomEquivL` equivalents, plus the definitions `bundleEquivL`/`tangentHomEquivL`) only typecheck because `(A.ofBaseSet h).ofBaseSet A.closure_dom_subset_baseSet` is definitionally `A`. No lemma states this, so after these simp lemmas rewrite, the result has type `SobolevSection ((A.ofBaseSet h).ofBaseSet _)`. Chart lemmas stated for `A` then no longer match syntactically, and consumers must rely on defeq.",
